      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If such sophisticated technology were embedded, the evidence would likely be subtle, not obvious. Look for extremely localized, faint electromagnetic hums or unusual, consistent thermal signatures emanating from the pots themselves, especially when the library is quiet. Certain types of fiber optic sensors might introduce minuscule, patterned light refractions around the base of the plants, though this would require specialized equipment to detect. Any consistent, low-level radio frequency interference that correlates precisely with the plant clusters would be a strong indicator of hidden signal collection.",
